<title>BELGIUM: Italy move does not change Swedish position.</title>
<headline>Italy move does not change Swedish position.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's re-entry into the European Union's exchange rate mechanism (ERM) does not change Sweden's position on not joining, Swedish Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;Our attitude (on the ERM) has not changed because of today's decision,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Asbrink reiterated that joining the ERM was not on Sweden's agenda.</p>
<p>After Sunday's decision by EU finance ministers that the lira could rejoin the ERM after a four-year absence, only Sweden, Britain and Greece remain outside the currency grid among EU countries.</p>
</text>
